  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math> be distinct integers where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>25</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>25</mn></math>. Then, the number of ways of choosing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>, such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></math> is divisible by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> , is _____ ."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "120",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p><p>And,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;are distinct integers.</p><p>Let</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>k</mi></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>N</mi></math></p><p>So, we have</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math>Number of ways</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></math>&nbsp;i.e,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>25</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></math>&nbsp;i.e,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>25</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Since,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;are distinct integers, so we cannot pair&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;i.e.,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>21</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;i.e.,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>14</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;i.e,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>22</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;i.e.,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>23</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;i.e.,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>23</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;i.e,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>22</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;i.e.,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>14</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;i.e,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>21</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>Total number of ways&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn></math></p>"
  }
